id:                     E3176
trigger_tool:           runtime|test|pipe|fork|conan
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        pipe\(pipe2\) == -2|fork was called after the second pipe failed|partial pipe set|EMFILE.*fork

severity:               2
category:               ipc-resource-failure-atomicity
match_keywords:         pipe, fork, exec, EMFILE, RLIMIT_NOFILE, staged resource acquisition, failure atomicity, rollback, file descriptor, syscall substitution, side effect barrier, cvm
title:                  Multiple IPC resources must be acquired as a failure-atomic set before fork or another irreversible side effect

root_cause:             A staged IPC setup checks the second pipe failure against an impossible return value and enters fork with only the first pipe valid; the uninitialized second descriptor pair makes black-box behavior nondeterministic and can hide the control-flow violation behind the same final I/O error.
affected_scope:         C and C++ code that acquires two or more pipes, socketpairs, event descriptors, files, or handles before starting a child, thread, callback, or registration step whose effects cannot be rolled back safely.
verification_cmd:       conan create archives/c/cvm/0.97 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=cvm/*

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           staged-acquisition-with-pre-side-effect-commit-barrier
rec_description:        Check every acquisition against its documented failure value; after an intermediate failure, release previously acquired resources in reverse order; enter fork/thread/register only after the complete resource set is valid. Pair an installed-artifact resource-limit test with deterministic compilation-unit syscall substitution that injects every acquisition/fork failure and records exact close order; also verify the successful parent transfers only the intended handles.
rec_command:            cc -I. -I$BGLIBS_INCLUDE tests/pipe_failure_atomic.c -o test-pipe-failure-atomic && ./test-pipe-failure-atomic; then run test_package/cvm_pipe_failure cvm_marker_helper MARKER against the packaged shared library
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               archives/c/cvm/0.97/patches/0001-client-xfer-command.c.patch and tests/pipe_failure_atomic.c

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      bounded-real-resource-exhaustion
fallback_description:   If symbol substitution is unavailable, lower RLIMIT_NOFILE in a fresh process, verify the documented error and audit descriptor/child side effects. This is weaker because uninitialized state can make a buggy version appear to return the same error.
fallback_command:       run cvm_pipe_failure in a fresh process with RLIMIT_NOFILE=5 and verify CVME_IO plus absence of the child marker
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          archives/c/cvm/0.97/test_package/test_pipe_failure.c

forbid_1_pattern:       assert only the final error code after partial acquisition|continue to fork after pipe failure|ignore cleanup for the first acquired descriptor pair
forbid_1_reason:        The final error can match by accident while resource leaks, invalid descriptor closes, or unintended child execution still occur.
forbid_1_consequence:   Flaky tests, descriptor corruption, child processes started with invalid standard streams, and latent leaks under resource pressure.

forbid_2_pattern:       force the production shared library static solely for fault injection|depend on uninitialized descriptor values
forbid_2_reason:        Changing the production link boundary or relying on undefined state invalidates the regression oracle.
forbid_2_consequence:   False red or false green results that do not describe the shipped artifact's control flow.

principles:               
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-cvm-0.97-two-pipe-failure-atomicity.md
last_updated:            2026-10-12
source_event:            cvm 0.97 HarmonyOS PC adaptation; second pipe EMFILE control-flow regression and revert-negative proof
